  "summaries": [
    {
      "id": 803080,
      "category": "team",
      "content": "##Security advisory: [REVIVE-SA-2026-001](https://www.revive-adserver.com/security/revive-sa-2026-001/)\n\n##Description\nHackerOne community member Faraz Ahmed (PakCyberbot) has reported a format string injection in the Revive Adserver settings. When specific character combinations are used in a setting, the admin user console could be disabled due to a fatal PHP error.\n \n##Details \nThe Revive Adserver settings are stored using INI files, which support variable interpolation. Using certain character sequences, such as `${{` in a setting was causing a PHP fatal error when reading back the configuration, due to inadequate escaping in the INI file writing classes from the PEAR_Config package. Only administrators are allowed to change settings, so, in normal circumstances, the disruption would be limited.",
      "updated_at": "2026-01-14T10:46:37.362Z",
